-- title:
--   Divisibility of idelic lattices versus integrality of n⁻¹g
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$ and write $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ for the associated quaternion algebra, $\mathbb{A}$ for the finite adèle ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ (the finite adèle ring of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$). Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ satisfying `IsOrder`, i.e. $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $\mathbb{H}$, and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated. Let $x,g$ be units of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}$ and let $n$ be a nonzero natural number. Here [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda$ is the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha\in\mathbb{A}$ having all components $\alpha_v$ in the ring of integers of the completion at each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, and [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda\,h$ is the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ of those $z$ whose image under $z\mapsto z\otimes 1$ lies in the left translate by $h$ of that box. The assertion is the equivalence: `ofFiniteIdele` $\Lambda\,(xg)$ is contained in the pointwise $\mathbb{Z}$-scalar multiple $(n:\mathbb{Z})\bullet$ `ofFiniteIdele` $\Lambda\,x$ if and only if $(n:\mathbb{Q})^{-1}\cdot g$ lies in `finiteAdeleBox` $\Lambda$.
--
--   This is the local–global bridge between the lattice-theoretic statement that the lattice cut out by the finite idèle $xg$ is divisible by $n$ inside the lattice cut out by $x$, and the idelic statement that $n^{-1}g$ is integral for $\Lambda$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd part of the development, where cyclicity of kernels of isogeny-type maps is translated into non-integrality conditions on finite idèles.
